<p>RETAIL TRADE - After detracting from growth in the June quarter, the strength seen in the first two months of the September quarter means that in the September quarter retail trade is likely to make a fairly large contribution to GDP, economists said. At the same time, the strength seen in the last two months also means that in the month of September, retail trade is likely to register a corrective fall, they said.</p>
